                    "reference": "Liu et al., J Neurooncol 2009",
                    "id": "19452021",
                    "type": "PMID",
                    "notes": "Glioblastoma cells expressing CD133 exhibit stem-like properties and heightened resistance to conventional therapy. CD133+ GSCs isolated from recurrent tumors can reform tumors, implicating them in post-treatment relapse ([pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8445366/#:~:text=cancer%20therapy%20resistance%20in%20high,grade%20gliomas))."
